# Files kept out of the Docker build context, so the image build is smaller, faster and cannot copy them in by accident.
# Build output: the image builds the binary itself, so a local build must not be sent.
target
# Dependencies of the page tooling; they are never part of the image.
**/node_modules
# Browser-test output from a local run.
page/test-results
page/playwright-report
# Repository history is not needed to build.
.git
# CI workflows are not part of the image.
.github
# Markdown documents are not part of the image...
*.md
# ...except the Profile Links specification, which the binary embeds and serves at the profile address.
!spec/*.md
# Local environment files can hold credentials; none may enter the build context.
.env*
